  "body": "Description:\r\nUpgrading matrixdotorg/synapse docker image from v.1.75 to v.1.76 results in the error: ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'shared_secret_authenticator'. Possibly missing python module.\r\n\r\nSteps to reproduce:\r\n1. Install latest matrix image & mount shared_secret_authenticator.py volume\r\n```\r\nsudo docker run -d --name matrix --restart unless-stopped \\\r\n    -v /path/Matrix/:/data \\\r\n    -v /path/Matrix/shared_secret_authenticator.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/shared_secret_authenticator.py \\\r\n    -p 8008:8008 \\\r\n    matrixdotorg/synapse:latest\r\n```\r\n\r\nShould return the error: ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'shared_secret_authenticator'\r\n\r\n2. Repeat the same by downgrading to v.1.75 & everything should work\r\n```\r\nsudo docker run -d --name matrix --restart unless-stopped \\\r\n    -v /path/Matrix/:/data \\\r\n    -v /path/Matrix/shared_secret_authenticator.py:/usr/local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/shared_secret_authenticator.py \\\r\n    -p 8008:8008 \\\r\n    matrixdotorg/synapse:v1.75.0\r\n```\r\n\r\nHomeserver\r\nLocal deployment with Docker\r\n\r\nSynapse Version\r\nv1.76.0\r\n\r\nInstallation Method\r\nDocker (matrixdotorg/synapse)\r\n\r\nDatabase\r\nPostgresql\r\n\r\nWorkers\r\nSingle process\r\n\r\nPlatform\r\nDocker engine running on Arch Linux\r\n\r\nConfiguration\r\nNo response\r\n\r\nAnything else I can share on this? \r\n\r\nThanks.\r\n\r\n",
